WEBVTT

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:38.413
This incredible victory has turned
the rumors on their head!

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:41.207
The 14th Platoon has shown
up the newly invigorated 17th

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.918
in truly veteran fashion!

00:00:56.056 --> 00:01:00.268
You rely too much on the new guy.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.689
Thank you for the battle!

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.033
<i>Brave your truth and brave yourself </i>

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:18.620
<i>So we can go somewhere with the dite</i>

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:28.546
<i>Keep hope alive, now we</i>
<i>wanna find the new world</i>

00:01:28.546 --> 00:01:31.883
<i>Roaming around the city having lost my map</i>

00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:35.220
<i>Even a dying world</i>

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:42.018
<i>Let me hear a life deep</i>
<i>within that won't stop running</i>

00:01:42.018 --> 00:01:45.021
<i>I seared the undying light into my eyes</i>

00:01:45.021 --> 00:01:48.566
<i>Refusing to shut them</i>
<i>even when they dried</i>

00:01:48.566 --> 00:01:55.281
<i>I don't believe anything I</i>
<i>can obtain without getting hurt</i>

00:01:55.281 --> 00:02:01.496
<i>A single emotion</i>
<i>directed toward someone</i>

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:08.753
<i>Splits the steel darkness</i>
<i>like the light of morning</i>

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:13.341
<i>One day brave your</i>
<i>truth and brave yourself</i>

00:02:13.341 --> 00:02:16.886
<i>So you will drastically change</i>

00:02:16.886 --> 00:02:22.726
<i>Compounded strength and prayers</i>

00:02:22.726 --> 00:02:26.479
<i>Intersecting futures</i>
<i>and wishes held close</i>

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:30.066
<i>I will give these to no one</i>

00:02:30.066 --> 00:02:31.568
<i>Just tough and alive</i>

00:02:31.568 --> 00:02:36.781
<i>It links our hearts</i>

00:02:46.916 --> 00:02:49.044
This is Layfon's?

00:02:49.044 --> 00:02:54.382
"Leerin"? Who's that?
That's a girl's name, isn't it?

00:02:54.382 --> 00:02:58.595
Is she Lay-ton's friend? Or his...

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:07.103
May! What are you doing?

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:15.695
Why May-cchi! What are you hiding, hmm?

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.405
N-Nothing!

00:03:17.405 --> 00:03:20.241
The eyes of Mii-<i>chan </i>cannot be deceived!

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:23.453
Now then! Spill the beans, all of it!

00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:26.331
It's really nothing, I'm telling you!

00:03:26.331 --> 00:03:27.165
Nakki!

00:03:27.165 --> 00:03:28.792
Yup.

00:03:36.007 --> 00:03:39.427
"The Letter From Glendan"

00:03:40.387 --> 00:03:42.847
This postmark is from Glendan, isn't it?

00:03:42.847 --> 00:03:47.268
I've heard of it. A lot of skilled
military artists come from there.

00:03:47.268 --> 00:03:51.523
Lay-ton really doesn't
talk about himself, does he?

00:03:51.523 --> 00:03:54.109
What should I do, now that this has happened?

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:55.151
I wonder if this is bad.

00:03:55.151 --> 00:03:57.153
It could be bad.

00:03:58.154 --> 00:03:59.781
Restoration.

00:04:00.824 --> 00:04:06.579
Maybe physical damage
has little to do with kei output.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.916
Will you keep transmitting kei like that for me?

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:11.543
Okay.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.671
It's too bad about the competition yesterday.

00:04:14.671 --> 00:04:16.548
Oh. Yeah.

00:04:16.548 --> 00:04:19.009
If you'd told Nina, we could've sat it out.

00:04:19.009 --> 00:04:20.593
It tarnishes the reputation.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:24.431
But all the platoons were mobilized.

00:04:32.397 --> 00:04:34.899
Are you really not pissed off?

00:04:34.899 --> 00:04:39.070
The only ones that know it was
you who took out all those larvals

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:42.699
are the 17th Platoon and a handful of others.

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:47.287
Most people think it was a group
effort that got us out of that.

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:50.206
And that's the truth. No doubt about it.

00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:52.500
No doubt about what?

00:04:53.543 --> 00:04:56.379
Harley, are they ready?

00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:59.674
Yes, yes. I made them as you requested.

00:04:59.674 --> 00:05:02.427
However, their firing range isn't...

00:05:02.427 --> 00:05:05.555
They're not for sniping, so I don't care.

00:05:05.555 --> 00:05:07.182
Restoration.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:12.145
Is that <i>jusho-jutsu</i>?

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:14.105
Hand-to-hand combat incorporating a gun.

00:05:14.105 --> 00:05:17.192
For a platoon like ours with few members,

00:05:17.192 --> 00:05:20.445
it's best if one person
can perform multiples roles, right?

00:05:20.445 --> 00:05:23.281
Still, probably the only
ones who actually do this stuff

00:05:23.281 --> 00:05:27.702
are skilled experts or idiots putting on airs.

00:05:28.703 --> 00:05:31.706
By the way, I'm in the "idiot" column.

00:05:36.378 --> 00:05:41.383
Did you do that in your former platoon as well?

00:05:41.383 --> 00:05:44.010
You were in another platoon.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.638
I remember hearing that
from Nina or somebody...

00:05:48.139 --> 00:05:50.141
That was like a year ago.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:52.811
Sorry.

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:54.312
What are you apologizing for?

00:05:54.312 --> 00:05:55.939
Uh, well...

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:15.083
My heart's pounding! I wish I hadn't said that!

00:06:15.083 --> 00:06:19.421
I... I think I'm going
to return this to Lay-ton.

00:06:19.421 --> 00:06:25.218
Huh? But you can't put all this on yourself.

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:29.222
No, I shouldn't have hidden this.

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:32.058
I want to give Lay-ton a proper apology.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:37.022
I'm such an idiot, trying to act brave...

00:06:38.189 --> 00:06:42.819
No, no! I decided I would
do this, so now I have to.

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:44.237
But...

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:46.698
"Hey, Lay-ton. Here's a letter."

00:06:46.698 --> 00:06:49.701
"Oh, Lay-ton! There's a letter to you from a
girl!"

00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:51.327
Um...

00:06:53.121 --> 00:06:56.166
You have something to see Layfon about?

00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:58.793
He should be inside.

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.004
You have plans to meet?

00:07:01.004 --> 00:07:03.089
You're waiting for him?

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:06.009
No, nothing like that! I was just passing by.

00:07:06.009 --> 00:07:10.305
Um, I have no real business
or anything like that.

00:07:10.305 --> 00:07:12.307
I'm sorry! My apologies for disturbing you.

00:07:12.307 --> 00:07:14.934
Sorry again, really, sorry!

00:07:19.564 --> 00:07:22.567
Leerin? Who is that?

00:07:24.527 --> 00:07:25.487
What's all that?

00:07:25.487 --> 00:07:28.823
Ah. There's something I wanted to confirm.

00:07:28.823 --> 00:07:30.700
Confirm?

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.078
What about Layfon is being "confirmed"?

00:07:33.078 --> 00:07:36.164
Beats me. I don't know what...

00:07:36.164 --> 00:07:39.793
This is about <i>you </i>and you don't know?

00:07:41.002 --> 00:07:43.296
Sorry I'm late.

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:46.591
So Nina's the last one? That's unusual.

00:07:46.591 --> 00:07:50.804
This is going nowhere
without our platoon leader.

00:07:57.018 --> 00:08:00.271
If we have no training,
I would like to return home.

00:08:00.271 --> 00:08:01.856
Sorry. I've kept you all waiting.

00:08:01.856 --> 00:08:04.442
Nina! You're late!

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:08.905
Don't worry about today's
training. I'm canceling it.

00:08:09.614 --> 00:08:14.619
You can train individually
however you like. Dismissed.

00:08:26.756 --> 00:08:28.967
Something's strange.

00:08:32.887 --> 00:08:35.515
Uh, with our leader.

00:08:36.266 --> 00:08:40.812
But all we can do is stay
silent and obey, correct?

00:08:40.812 --> 00:08:42.230
She...

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:46.276
I doubt she will voluntarily
offer any information.

00:08:46.276 --> 00:08:47.902
Yeah.

00:08:51.031 --> 00:08:53.658
Are you free today?

00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:58.621
Well, we don't have practice now, but...

00:08:58.621 --> 00:09:03.668
It seems my brother has something
to discuss with you in private.

00:09:03.668 --> 00:09:04.919
The student council president?

00:09:04.919 --> 00:09:09.799
I don't know what it is about,
but he said it is important.

00:09:11.926 --> 00:09:16.222
I must therefore buy ingredients
for this evening's dinner.

00:09:16.222 --> 00:09:18.224
Please accompany me.

00:09:24.105 --> 00:09:25.732
Ma'am?

00:09:26.775 --> 00:09:27.776
Felli!

00:09:27.984 --> 00:09:32.238
I am currently preparing food.
Please wait there.

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:33.865
Okay...

00:09:37.952 --> 00:09:39.371
What are you...?

00:09:39.371 --> 00:09:42.499
Please do not speak to me.

00:09:43.625 --> 00:09:45.335
Have you ever cooked before?

00:09:45.335 --> 00:09:47.504
Of course I have.

00:09:47.504 --> 00:09:49.130
Is that so?

00:09:50.298 --> 00:09:51.341
What is it?!

00:09:51.341 --> 00:09:53.218
Well, uh...

00:09:53.218 --> 00:09:59.391
I think peeling them <i>before </i>you
cut makes them easier to cook later.

00:10:03.478 --> 00:10:05.146
You enjoy cooking?

00:10:05.146 --> 00:10:08.274
Not so much "enjoy" as,
at the orphanage in Glendan

00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:10.860
cooking was something everyone did together.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:14.864
You cooked alongside girls as well, correct?

00:10:14.864 --> 00:10:18.493
Sure. Girls, boys, we all did whatever.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:28.044
This is quite delicious, Alseif-<i>kun</i>.

00:10:28.044 --> 00:10:30.255
My apologies for such humble fare...

00:10:30.255 --> 00:10:35.510
Not at all. I'm grateful for my first
home-cooked meal in some time.

00:10:36.136 --> 00:10:38.888
Is that-- Ow!

00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:42.100
It seems your wounds still pain you.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:42.892
No, I'm fine!

00:10:42.892 --> 00:10:45.562
Oh. My apologies for being late today.

00:10:45.562 --> 00:10:48.314
I was meeting with the
Chief of the Municipal Police.

00:10:48.314 --> 00:10:49.649
The municipal police?

00:10:49.649 --> 00:10:52.527
Yes. There was a slightly troubling matter

00:10:52.527 --> 00:10:55.905
and we had to prepare to delay
departure of the roaming buses.

00:10:55.905 --> 00:10:58.700
Oh, one of your friends

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:01.327
submitted a work application
to the municipal police.

00:11:01.327 --> 00:11:04.748
Naruki Gelni, I believe it was.

00:11:06.458 --> 00:11:09.294
Isn't there anywhere else
you could have dropped it?

00:11:09.294 --> 00:11:12.380
I had it while I was waiting for him...

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:14.299
It doesn't look like it's been

00:11:14.299 --> 00:11:16.676
submitted to the municipal
police's lost and found.

00:11:18.345 --> 00:11:21.473
Is it all right if I try talking to Lay-ton?

00:11:22.724 --> 00:11:24.726
Why you, Nakki?

00:11:25.185 --> 00:11:28.229
I have something else
to talk to Lay-ton about as well.

00:11:28.229 --> 00:11:30.523
I'd like you to take a look at this.

00:11:30.523 --> 00:11:33.109
It took some time, but I've
now been made fully aware

00:11:33.109 --> 00:11:35.862
of the need to consider
defenses outside the city.

00:11:35.862 --> 00:11:38.448
As an experiment,
we launched an unmanned probe.

00:11:38.448 --> 00:11:41.201
This was taken approximately 500 kilmels

00:11:41.201 --> 00:11:44.079
further along Zuellni's current route.

00:11:44.079 --> 00:11:45.997
What do you think?

00:11:47.082 --> 00:11:49.584
I believe it's just as you fear.

00:11:49.584 --> 00:11:51.586
What is this?

00:11:51.586 --> 00:11:53.797
It's a male contaminoid.

00:11:54.756 --> 00:11:55.799
So Harley...

00:11:55.799 --> 00:11:59.928
Or rather, the Alchemy
Department's lab confirmed my kei

00:11:59.928 --> 00:12:01.471
for this reason?

00:12:01.471 --> 00:12:03.848
You're quite perceptive. That's helpful.

00:12:03.848 --> 00:12:07.560
I'm not being sarcastic. This is honest praise.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:08.853
Brother!

00:12:08.853 --> 00:12:12.691
Do you intend to use him again?

00:12:12.691 --> 00:12:16.403
Till now, Zuellni has been a peaceful city.

00:12:16.403 --> 00:12:17.904
But for some reason...

00:12:17.904 --> 00:12:21.950
it now continually seeks
to encounter the contaminoids.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:26.121
I don't know why this is,
but one thing I know clearly

00:12:26.121 --> 00:12:29.749
is that our only way to
survive is to rely on him.

00:12:39.217 --> 00:12:41.469
I'm gonna take them out.

00:12:41.469 --> 00:12:43.555
Remember the time limit.

00:12:43.555 --> 00:12:45.181
I know.

00:12:56.526 --> 00:12:59.904
So... Something the boss didn't consider, hm?

00:12:59.904 --> 00:13:01.031
Saya! Gun me!

00:13:01.031 --> 00:13:02.657
Here.

00:13:06.661 --> 00:13:10.665
Coming after me wasn't your best decision.

00:13:18.298 --> 00:13:23.303
Thank you for the meal today,
Senio... Uh, Felli.

00:13:23.303 --> 00:13:24.929
Fon-Fon?

00:13:26.765 --> 00:13:28.850
No, nothing.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:30.852
See you tomorrow.

00:13:31.895 --> 00:13:35.023
<i>The really frightening ones are the elders.</i>

00:13:35.023 --> 00:13:36.524
<i>Elders?</i>

00:13:36.524 --> 00:13:39.110
<i>Contaminoids that have ceased to reproduce.</i>

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:43.239
<i>They grow stronger with each passing year.</i>

00:13:43.239 --> 00:13:49.245
<i>Have you defeated one before?</i>
<i>One of these "elders"?</i>

00:13:49.245 --> 00:13:53.625
<i>As part of a trio.</i>
<i>I thought we were going to die.</i>

00:13:58.213 --> 00:14:00.548
Welcome back, Lay-ton.

00:14:00.548 --> 00:14:04.719
What brings you here at this hour?
How long have you... Are you alone?

00:14:04.719 --> 00:14:08.765
Yeah. I wanted to ask, did you
get anything in the mail recently?

00:14:08.765 --> 00:14:11.434
In the mail? Like a present?

00:14:11.434 --> 00:14:14.604
I guess. Something like that.

00:14:14.604 --> 00:14:18.066
No, I don't think so.

00:14:18.066 --> 00:14:19.693
Oh...

00:14:20.026 --> 00:14:24.656
Fail! I can't hear anything they're saying!

00:14:27.117 --> 00:14:31.538
That's the leader of Lay-ton's
platoon, isn't it?

00:14:31.538 --> 00:14:33.540
What, this late?

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.126
One more thing?

00:14:36.126 --> 00:14:41.339
Yeah. For me, this could
be the more important topic...

00:14:42.507 --> 00:14:47.554
The truth is, I wondered if you
could help me with a police job.

00:14:47.554 --> 00:14:48.888
Me?

00:14:48.888 --> 00:14:52.809
They have a "special dispatch" system, and...

00:14:52.809 --> 00:14:58.440
The division head, my boss,
found out that I knew you

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:02.652
and told me to ask you. What do you think?

00:15:02.652 --> 00:15:04.404
Uh, well...

00:15:04.404 --> 00:15:08.074
I know! You're in the Military Arts,
assigned to a platoon

00:15:08.074 --> 00:15:09.826
and you work cleaning the machinery department.

00:15:09.826 --> 00:15:14.247
So feel free to decline.
But if you could help just a little...

00:15:14.247 --> 00:15:18.918
If I refused, would it be bad for you?

00:15:18.918 --> 00:15:21.296
They wouldn't reject your
work application or something?

00:15:21.296 --> 00:15:26.134
They wouldn't! Uh, do that... I think...

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:33.641
Personally, I think it'd be nice
if you were on special dispatch.

00:15:33.641 --> 00:15:36.227
Can I think about it a little?

00:15:36.227 --> 00:15:38.063
Of course!

00:15:53.411 --> 00:15:55.205
U-Um...

00:15:55.205 --> 00:15:56.456
Yes?

00:15:56.456 --> 00:15:59.250
Um... Yesterday...

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:01.878
You want something?

00:16:02.295 --> 00:16:05.507
If this is about that letter,
I already returned it.

00:16:06.424 --> 00:16:09.969
U-Um, thank you very much! Really, thank--

00:16:09.969 --> 00:16:12.972
Not at all. I'm in a hurry.

00:16:14.224 --> 00:16:16.226
Why did I say that?

00:16:40.583 --> 00:16:44.379
Don't go heading back on your own,
Felli-<i>chan</i>. It's lonely, right?

00:16:44.379 --> 00:16:47.382
I don't like to stay for long
periods where the sun is bright.

00:16:47.382 --> 00:16:50.260
That will be all for today. Dismissed.

00:16:51.094 --> 00:16:55.724
Well done, everyone. If you'll excuse me.

00:16:57.183 --> 00:16:58.935
Someone's in a rush to leave.

00:16:58.935 --> 00:17:01.104
I'll be using the shower
if ya don't mind, Layfon.

00:17:01.104 --> 00:17:03.773
Go ahead. I still have some training to do.

00:17:03.773 --> 00:17:07.027
Layfon, you can go ahead and leave too.

00:17:07.027 --> 00:17:10.071
We're going to stop training
in tandem techniques for a while.

00:17:10.071 --> 00:17:12.615
Why? Is there a problem with how I've...?

00:17:12.615 --> 00:17:14.743
I've simply decided it's not necessary.

00:17:14.743 --> 00:17:17.537
Oh. Okay...

00:17:17.537 --> 00:17:22.083
Well, I'll take a shower
first, if that's all right.

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.845
Leerin? Who's that?

00:17:35.013 --> 00:17:36.431
Many thanks!

00:17:36.431 --> 00:17:39.434
It's a big help. I'm Formed Garen,

00:17:39.434 --> 00:17:41.895
head of the Municipal Police Security Division.

00:17:41.895 --> 00:17:42.854
A pleasure.

00:17:42.854 --> 00:17:45.857
To get right to it, are you free tonight?

00:17:45.857 --> 00:17:49.402
Uh, I have to clean the machinery department,

00:17:49.402 --> 00:17:52.572
but if you can manage something with them...

00:17:52.572 --> 00:17:57.410
Okay! I'll talk with them myself.
You head out with Naruki.

00:17:58.661 --> 00:18:00.663
Countin' on ya.

00:18:01.373 --> 00:18:05.210
They're disguised as a caravan
selling magazines and digifilms

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:08.755
but the truth is, they've
come to steal Zuellni's information.

00:18:08.755 --> 00:18:11.299
What proof do we have that they're criminals?

00:18:11.299 --> 00:18:13.343
There's an eyewitness.

00:18:13.927 --> 00:18:17.347
We've tried stopping the roaming
buses, but we've reached the limit.

00:18:17.347 --> 00:18:19.849
They're planning to break their way out.

00:18:19.849 --> 00:18:23.019
Yeah. The student council
president mentioned that.

00:18:23.019 --> 00:18:24.979
You spoke with the student council president?!

00:18:24.979 --> 00:18:28.858
He just called me about something.
That's when he mentioned it.

00:18:28.858 --> 00:18:33.279
I'm sorry. Forcing you to help
when you have so much to deal with...

00:18:33.279 --> 00:18:36.491
Not at all. I was the one who agreed.

00:18:36.491 --> 00:18:40.078
No, I mean... This was
an underhanded negotiation.

00:18:40.078 --> 00:18:41.996
We pushed you so that you couldn't refuse.

00:18:41.996 --> 00:18:45.417
Having something
I can do to help is a good thing.

00:18:45.417 --> 00:18:49.754
No! You probably don't know this,
but the elite platoon members

00:18:49.754 --> 00:18:53.675
would <i>never </i>go on the
municipal police's special dispatch.

00:18:53.675 --> 00:18:56.428
I don't know about other platoon members,

00:18:56.428 --> 00:19:01.016
but personally, being needed makes me happy.

00:19:14.446 --> 00:19:16.865
Give it up!

00:19:19.492 --> 00:19:22.495
Five of them... All of them quite skilled.

00:19:22.495 --> 00:19:24.247
I'm going in first.

00:19:24.247 --> 00:19:26.249
Restoration-01!

00:19:41.306 --> 00:19:42.932
This way.

00:19:43.183 --> 00:19:45.602
You did a great job.

00:19:45.602 --> 00:19:48.730
What will happen to the culprits?

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:52.108
They'll be made to wear convicts'
clothes, put on a roaming bus and exiled.

00:19:52.108 --> 00:19:54.569
All their belongings will be confiscated.

00:19:54.569 --> 00:19:55.945
Including those data chips.

00:19:55.945 --> 00:19:59.240
I wonder what price all those will fetch.

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:01.576
Sir, you plan to sell them?

00:20:01.576 --> 00:20:03.495
Is there a problem with that?

00:20:03.495 --> 00:20:06.581
It's impossible to return
them to the original owners.

00:20:06.581 --> 00:20:10.877
At least we can use them for Zuellni's benefit.

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:16.091
Oh, Naruki, you did excellent work today.

00:20:16.091 --> 00:20:20.804
I think you'll receive a hiring notice
from the municipal police in the next few days.

00:20:20.804 --> 00:20:22.806
Thank you very much.

00:20:23.223 --> 00:20:25.392
I don't think he's a bad person.

00:20:25.392 --> 00:20:29.688
I know, but... His attitude toward the money,

00:20:29.688 --> 00:20:33.525
or the way he didn't try to hide it...
I don't know about that.

00:20:33.525 --> 00:20:35.235
I think it shows principles.

00:20:35.235 --> 00:20:37.404
Principles?! How?

00:20:37.404 --> 00:20:41.741
He doesn't think that what he does is wrong.

00:20:41.741 --> 00:20:46.746
I think that shows
principles and a lot of strength.

00:20:47.622 --> 00:20:50.625
By the way, what was that you
said about something in the mail?

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:55.880
Oh! Uh...

00:20:57.674 --> 00:20:58.925
It stopped!

00:20:58.925 --> 00:21:00.343
It looks like Zuellni's gone.

00:21:00.343 --> 00:21:01.052
Again?!

00:21:01.052 --> 00:21:04.347
Where's Nina? She could track Zuellni down.

00:21:04.347 --> 00:21:08.852
That whimsical electronic
spirit is a pain in the ass!

00:21:10.854 --> 00:21:13.356
You sneaked out again did you, Zuellni?

00:21:13.356 --> 00:21:15.567
You're incorrigible, aren't you?

00:21:19.612 --> 00:21:22.323
It's a letter. To Layfon.

00:21:24.451 --> 00:21:27.454
No, you can't read it.

00:21:28.204 --> 00:21:31.708
I understand how you feel though.

00:21:33.209 --> 00:21:34.836
Zuellni.

00:21:36.254 --> 00:21:40.467
I... I'll get stronger.

00:21:42.052 --> 00:21:44.471
In the locker room?

00:21:44.846 --> 00:21:48.808
Yes. I thought I'd give it
to you at work last night, but...

00:21:48.808 --> 00:21:52.270
Oh! I'm sorry for suddenly taking the day off.

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:57.192
Don't worry about it.
Well, I gave it to you, so bye.

00:22:02.697 --> 00:22:05.950
Were you awake? I'm glad.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:10.372
Can you come to the Military Training Hall now?

00:22:35.271 --> 00:22:38.024
<i>Beyond memory</i>

00:22:38.024 --> 00:22:46.449
<i>A map of the ideal future</i>
<i>you'd been searching for</i>

00:22:46.449 --> 00:22:57.669
<i>Scared of something, not</i>
<i>understanding, trembling alone</i>

00:22:57.669 --> 00:23:08.888
<i>Unable to see you, I'm</i>
<i>always wearing a fake smile</i>

00:23:08.888 --> 00:23:18.023
<i>I was held in your arms</i>

00:23:18.023 --> 00:23:23.653
<i>Fall in love like</i>
<i>you're waking up</i>

00:23:23.653 --> 00:23:29.034
<i>And then take</i>
<i>me into dreamland</i>

00:23:29.034 --> 00:23:34.789
<i>You always, you always</i>

00:23:34.789 --> 00:23:44.966
<i>You always told me tender lies</i>

00:23:53.975 --> 00:23:56.019
<i>Nina, wanting to approach Layfon's strength,</i>

00:23:56.019 --> 00:23:58.855
<i>uses her kei to its very limit and collapses.</i>

00:23:58.855 --> 00:24:02.484
<i>Layfon leaves Nina with what</i>
<i>could be taken as his last testament</i>

00:24:02.484 --> 00:24:04.861
<i>and attempts to face the contaminoids alone.</i>

00:24:04.861 --> 00:24:06.780
<i>Next time, "Adamandite Restored," and...</i>

00:24:06.780 --> 00:24:08.128
<i>Restoration!</i>
